## Project Structure

Layered or hexagonal, enforced by the crate graph. A single crate with the same top-level modules is acceptable for small services.

```
{{PROJECT_NAME}}/
├── Cargo.toml                    # [workspace], [workspace.dependencies], [workspace.lints]
├── Cargo.lock                    # Committed (binary)
├── rust-toolchain.toml           # Pinned channel + clippy + rustfmt
├── deny.toml                     # cargo-deny policy
├── crates/
│   ├── domain/                   # Entities, value objects, errors, ports (no axum/sqlx/tokio)
│   ├── application/              # Use cases, orchestration
│   ├── infrastructure/           # sqlx repositories, external clients, config
│   ├── http/                     # axum routers, handlers, extractors, AppError, middleware
│   └── app/                      # Binary: config, pool, router, server, graceful shutdown
│
├── migrations/                   # sqlx migrations (forward-only)
├── .sqlx/                        # Offline query cache (cargo sqlx prepare)
├── tests/                        # Cross-crate integration tests (oneshot, sqlx::test)
├── docker/                       # Docker configuration
├── docs/                         # Documentation and ADRs
└── scripts/ci.sh                 # fmt, clippy, sqlx check, nextest, deny, audit
```

